The Desktop App speaks the intercom protocol of Kiosk Satellite and of Intercom Satellite for
Android (https://github.com/meiser79/intercom-satellite).

It uses Qt 6 (https://www.qt.io), licensed under the GNU LGPL v3, and FFmpeg's libavcodec,
libavutil and libswscale (https://ffmpeg.org), licensed under the GNU LGPL v2.1 or later; a
distribution build of FFmpeg may be licensed under the GNU GPL. H.264 encoding uses the encoder
FFmpeg provides, usually x264 (GNU GPL v2 or later). Its TLS certificate is made with OpenSSL's
libcrypto (https://www.openssl.org), licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

The button icons are Material Icons by Google (https://fonts.google.com/icons), licensed under
the Apache License 2.0, the same as in the Android app. The room icons are Material Design Icons by
Pictogrammers (https://pictogrammers.com/library/mdi/), also licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
